Additional Rules That Complete The Picture:
11. SOLID Principles Throughout
Single Responsibility, Open/Closed, Liskov Substitution, Interface Segregation, Dependency Inversion
12. Fail Fast & Defensive Programming
Validate early, throw meaningful exceptions, guard clauses at method entry
13. Async All The Way
No .Result or .Wait() - async/await from top to bottom
ConfigureAwait(false) in library code
14. Immutability By Default
readonly fields, init properties, record types where appropriate
Minimize mutable state
15. Resource Management
using statements for IDisposable, proper async disposal patterns
16. Performance-Conscious Design
Span<T>, Memory<T> for high-perf scenarios
Avoid allocations in hot paths
17. Exception Strategy
Domain-specific exceptions, never catch Exception unless rethrowing
Log before throwing (structured logging)
18. Thread-Safe By Design
Concurrent collections, proper locking patterns, avoid shared mutable state